  <a name="5.4"> </a>
  <a name="5.4.0"> </a>
  <h3>Release 5.4.0</h3>
  <ul>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-43595">FHIR-43595</a>: Improve change tracking in the extension registry</li>
   <li>The DocumentReference extensions <a href="StructureDefinition-documentreference-sourcepatient.html">documentreference-sourcepatient</a> and <a href="StructureDefinition-documentreference-thumbnail.html">documentreference-thumbnail</a> are now owned by FHIR Infrastructure (previously Orders and Observations)</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-59432">FHIR-39327</a>: Mark artifact-versionAlgorithm, elementdefinition-suppress, patient-sexParameterForClinicalUse, quantity-confidenceInterval, questionnaire-derivationType, rdf-concept-iri and structuredefinition-imposeProfile as active</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-57719">FHIR-57719</a>: Add CapabilityStatement.instantiates as a context for the <a href="StructureDefinition-capabilitystatement-expectation.html">Conformance expectation</a> extension</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-57837">FHIR-57837</a>: The minimum value of the <a href="StructureDefinition-questionnaire-maxOccurs.html">maxOccurs</a> extension is now 2 (a repeating item must allow at least 2 repetitions)</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-57839">FHIR-57839</a>: The minimum value of the <a href="StructureDefinition-questionnaire-minOccurs.html">minOccurs</a> extension is now 1 (it only applies to required items)</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-57563">FHIR-57563</a>: New extension <a href="StructureDefinition-media-representation.html">media-representation</a> - a media representation (e.g. a scanned fax, an audio clip) of the target of a Reference or canonical. Media is a target for the versions where it exists (R4B and earlier), using version-specific-use on the target profile</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-56001">FHIR-56001</a>: Add Ratio as a context for the <a href="StructureDefinition-rendered-value.html">rendered-value</a> extension, for ratios with a preferred rendering (e.g. 33/99 shown as 1/3)</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-53267">FHIR-53267</a>: Add RelatedArtifact as a context for the <a href="StructureDefinition-package-source.html">package-source</a> extension, so the source package of a dependency can be recorded during a dependency walk</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-58610">FHIR-58610</a>: New extensions <a href="StructureDefinition-additional-operation-context.html">additional-operation-context</a>, <a href="StructureDefinition-additional-operation-parameter-allowedType.html">additional-operation-parameter-allowedType</a> and <a href="StructureDefinition-additional-operation-parameter-targetProfile.html">additional-operation-parameter-targetProfile</a>, so an additional resource can supplement existing operation definitions</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-57235">FHIR-57235</a>: Add ValueSet.compose.include.concept as a context for the <a href="StructureDefinition-structuredefinition-standards-status.html">standards-status</a> extension, so it can replace the deprecated valueset-deprecated extension there</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-59372">FHIR-59372</a>: The <a href="StructureDefinition-originalText.html">originalText</a> extension notes that it can accompany a value or components, but can also be sent in place of a primitive value or components</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-58619">FHIR-58619</a>: New search parameter <a href="SearchParameter-artifact-topic.html">topic</a> for the <a href="StructureDefinition-artifact-topic.html">artifact-topic</a> extension</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-58616">FHIR-58616</a>: New extension <a href="StructureDefinition-alternate-title.html">alternate-title</a> (alternative human labels for an artifact, e.g. acronyms and short titles), and search parameter <a href="SearchParameter-any-title.html">any-title</a> that searches the title and alternate titles</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-57615">FHIR-57615</a>: New extension <a href="StructureDefinition-operationoutcome-resource.html">operationoutcome-resource</a> - identifies the source resource related to an OperationOutcome or one of its issues (e.g. the resource that an issue.expression is rooted in)</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-56002">FHIR-56002</a>: New extensions <a href="StructureDefinition-thumbnail.html">thumbnail</a> (a smaller version of the content of an Attachment, e.g. for preview) and <a href="StructureDefinition-isThumbnail.html">isThumbnail</a> (marks an Attachment in a repeating element as a low-resolution form of the content). The <a href="StructureDefinition-documentreference-thumbnail.html">documentreference-thumbnail</a> extension is deprecated in favour of isThumbnail</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-44354">FHIR-44354</a>: The <a href="StructureDefinition-workflow-protectiveFactor.html">workflow-protectiveFactor</a> and <a href="StructureDefinition-workflow-barrier.html">workflow-barrier</a> extensions note that they are not workflow-related despite their names, and protectiveFactor explains why its contexts are limited to prospective care</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-57265">FHIR-57265</a>: New extension <a href="StructureDefinition-contentReferenceProfile.html">contentReferenceProfile</a> - a profile (element) that applies to an element defined by a contentReference, so that profile constraints on recursive elements such as Questionnaire.item can be applied at nested levels</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-56953">FHIR-56953</a>: The <a href="StructureDefinition-largeValue.html">largeValue</a> extension allows integer64 as well as decimal for its value</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-56447">FHIR-56447</a>: The <a href="StructureDefinition-package-source.html">package-source</a> extension is marked (snapshot-behavior = ignore) so that it is not copied into derived profiles</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-56412">FHIR-56412</a>: New extension <a href="StructureDefinition-suppress-actor.html">suppress-actor</a> - identifies an actor that is not relevant for the current publication, so its obligations are not prominently shown in profile tables or used to determine key elements</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-39327">FHIR-39327</a>: In the <a href="StructureDefinition-relative-date.html">relative-date</a> extension, targetReference and targetCode are each optional, with an invariant that at least one is present, and documentation of how they combine</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-55397">FHIR-55397</a>: Clarified the <a href="StructureDefinition-obligation.html">obligation</a> extension's applicable-number - it sets the minimum number of repetitions a system must support for that obligation - and documented how obligations apply to repeating elements</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-55398">FHIR-55398</a>: Documented how obligations can depend on context (clinical context, relevance, business rules) - via the usage property, slicing, profile scope, and implementation context</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-52992">FHIR-52992</a>: Removed CodeSystem.concept as a context for the <a href="StructureDefinition-structuredefinition-standards-status.html">standards-status</a> extension - the status of a concept is represented using a concept property</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-50851">FHIR-50851</a>: New extension <a href="StructureDefinition-reserved-code-space.html">reserved-code-space</a> - describes a set of codes (by regular expression) that the code system steward has allocated for users to create their own codes</li>
   <li><a href="https://jira.hl7.org/browse/FHIR-53122">FHIR-53122</a>: New extension <a href="StructureDefinition-valueset-scope.html">valueset-scope</a> - replaces the R5 ValueSet.scope element (inclusionCriteria, exclusionCriteria), which has been removed in R6</li>
  </ul>
